+      "delta": "The full-text-backed LeFlow record replaces repeated CEM search with rectified-flow latent trajectory generation, inverse-dynamics decoding, and frozen-LeWM rollout reranking, whereas RankCal leaves the planner and latent backbone fixed and changes the numerical PTQ calibration/allocation signal to preserve candidate ordering under multi-step quantized rollouts."
+    },
+    {
+      "paper_id": "arxiv:2607.28405v1",
+      "delta": "The connector-verified but abstract-only adjacent QuantWAMs record proposes coordinate-compatible activation evidence, joint video-action saliency, and fixed-intervention auditing for WAM PTQ, whereas RankCal targets latent-dynamics planner rankings without WAM future/action coupling and derives weight/activation bits from site-only ranking influence."
+    }
+  ],
+  "almost_prior_paper_id": "arxiv:2602.02110v1",
+  "what_step_was_missed": "It would have needed to hold candidate pools, planner inputs, receding-horizon conventions, and tie rules fixed while quantizing one site at a time, estimate that site's candidate-order discordance over action-conditioned rollout states, and solve the resulting profile as a memory-constrained mixed W/A assignment; the supplied method constructs PTQ sweeps and outcome analyses but not this decision-influence object or allocation step.",
